+### vaapi_vbv_frames
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            How many frames' worth of bitrate a single frame may use (the VBV/HRD buffer size in frames).
+            1 keeps every frame within one frame's share of the bitrate, which leaves a scene change coarse
+            until the picture moves again; larger values let the first frame after a scene change use more bits.
+            @note{This option applies to VA-API on Intel GPUs, AV1, or when [vaapi_strict_rc_buffer](#vaapi_strict_rc_buffer) is enabled.}
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            1
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            vaapi_vbv_frames = 4
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
+### vaapi_rc_mode
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Rate control mode for the frame-limited VBV path. Auto uses VBR with a 1-frame VBV and CBR
+            with a larger one. CBR keeps spending bits on still frames so they sharpen over time; VBR does not.
+            @note{This option applies to VA-API on Intel GPUs, AV1, or when [vaapi_strict_rc_buffer](#vaapi_strict_rc_buffer) is enabled.}
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            0
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Choices</td>
+        <td>0</td>
+        <td>auto</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td></td>
+        <td>1</td>
+        <td>VBR</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td></td>
+        <td>2</td>
+        <td>CBR</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td></td>
+        <td>3</td>
+        <td>CQP (every frame at [qp](#qp), no bitrate limit)</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            vaapi_rc_mode = 2
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
+### vaapi_max_qp
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Highest quantizer (1-51) the driver's rate control may use; 0 keeps the driver default. A lower
+            value is a quality floor: the first frame after a scene change cannot be coarser than this, at the
+            cost of exceeding the bitrate for that frame. Not used in CQP mode.
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            0
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            vaapi_max_qp = 30
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
+### vaapi_min_qp
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Lowest quantizer (1-51) the driver's rate control may use; 0 keeps the driver default. Not used in
+            CQP mode.
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            0
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            vaapi_min_qp = 18
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
+### vaapi_low_power
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Which VA-API encode entrypoint to use. Auto prefers the low power (LP) entrypoint when the driver
+            offers it; 0 forces the full encoder; 1 uses only the LP entrypoint.
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            -1
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Choices</td>
+        <td>-1</td>
+        <td>auto</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td></td>
+        <td>0</td>
+        <td>full encoder</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td></td>
+        <td>1</td>
+        <td>LP only</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            vaapi_low_power = 0
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
